  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 AM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures across the region are in the upper 50s \nto low 60s with relatively calm winds out of the northwest to north. \nHigh pressure is in place again today with a low off to our west. \nThe daylight hours today will be dry, and there is a slight chance \nof some showers/storms after midnight. These precipitation chances \nincrease to about 25-30% after sunrise and last through the \nafternoon. Chances increase again to 50-75% Friday evening mainly \neast of the Missouri River as the low off to our west moves into the \nregion. There is a Marginal risk (level 1 out of 5) for severe \nstorms east of the MO river. Hazards will be 1 inch hail and 60 mph \nwind gusts. This low will continue to move slowly across the area \nSaturday, finally exiting the region late Sunday. Precipitation \nchances remain during this time frame. Monday looks to be dry with \nsome slight chances for precipitation returning Tuesday through the \nend of the forecast.\n\nTemperatures continue the around average trend of the last several \ndays with highs generally in the high 70s to 80s, perhaps reaching \n90 west river Friday and Saturday. There could be a slight haze\nto the sky today and Friday as another round of elevated smoke \nmakes its way across the region. Winds with that incoming low \nwill be in the 25-35 mph range Friday afternoon mainly in \ncentral SD.",
